# 7. AI-BASED DYNAMIC REROUTING

When Camera 2 detects congestion, the edge module should publish a traffic event.

The backend should:

1. Verify the event source and freshness.
2. Determine which road segment is affected.
3. Update the relevant traffic estimate.
4. Recalculate candidate routes.
5. Compare the new ETA against the current route.
6. Ignore insignificant fluctuations to avoid constant rerouting.
7. Recommend a change only when supported by the available data.
8. Update the ambulance and hospital dashboards.
9. Recalculate checkpoint order.
10. Deactivate obsolete checkpoint requests safely.
11. Activate the next eligible checkpoint on the new route.

The ambulance operator must receive a clear explanation of the recommendation.

Do not reroute based on a single unverified detection. Include a confidence threshold, freshness check, and fallback when data is unavailable.

